WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.770
Speaker 1: So in all likelihood, Donald Trump
is not nearly as rich as he claims to be.

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:10.950
We know that Donald Trump inflates the value
of his real estate when it's for the purposes

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:16.710
of claiming a higher net worth or when it's
for the purposes of securing a loan, but minimizes

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:21.340
the value of his real estate when it's an
effort to avoid taxation.

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:26.480
But this story is just kind of weird because
presumably Donald Trump is a billionaire.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:28.640
The question is, to what degree is he a billionaire?

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:34.510
And yet in the last few months, Donald Trump
has taken sixty five thousand dollars in optional

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:40.370
federal pension payments for former presidents
since he left office in January.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:45.480
And you might recall that during his presidency,
Trump made a very big deal out of donating

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:50.199
his presidential salary back to different
federal agencies, maybe some charities, maybe

00:00:50.199 --> 00:00:51.650
it was just agencies.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:54.750
And he doesn't need the money and all of that
different stuff.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:01:02.989
And yet billionaire Donald Trump is now taking
sixty five thousand dollars from the presidential

00:01:02.989 --> 00:01:04.170
pension fund.

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:09.020
Now, you might remember the congressional,
but not the congressional.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:14.990
The Constitution requires that presidents
take a salary while in office.

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:17.280
They can donate it back fine.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:21.950
But there's nothing constitutionally that
says an ex-president must take their pension.

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:26.509
Now, this is, of course, completely within
Trump's rights to do.

00:01:26.509 --> 00:01:30.870
But I find it strange to some degree, because
if you look at a more realistic estimate of

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:36.270
Donald Trump's net worth, it's two point three
billion dollars relative to two point three

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:37.910
billion dollars.

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.869
Sixty five thousand dollars is point zero
zero to eight percent of his net worth.

00:01:43.869 --> 00:01:49.979
So to think about it in in terms that might
be more applicable to the average person,

00:01:49.979 --> 00:01:54.340
this is equivalent to someone with the median
American net worth, which is one hundred and

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:59.979
twenty one thousand dollars going through
a process to request three dollars and 40

00:01:59.979 --> 00:02:00.979
cents.

00:02:00.979 --> 00:02:02.000
Think about that for a second.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:06.409
If you retire from a job or you get laid off
or whatever, and someone comes to you and

00:02:06.409 --> 00:02:10.910
they say, sir, if you want, you can request
a pension.

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:16.110
You go through this process and we'll give
you three dollars and 40 cents.

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:20.390
Would most people go through that trouble
if their net worth is one hundred and twenty

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:21.900
one thousand dollars?

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:24.430
That's what Donald Trump is doing here.

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:25.430
So what's going on?

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:30.360
I mean, it reminds me of people who go to
the bank to cash a check for 12 cents.

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:36.080
The upside is by taking this, he seems to
recognize he's no longer the president because

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:39.170
this is a federal pension for ex presidents.

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:42.150
So maybe that's sort of like an upside here.

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:44.520
And being a former president comes with many
perks.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:47.120
There's lifetime Secret Service protection.

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:50.420
There's travel reimbursements, there's medical
insurance, there's a budget for an office

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:54.540
and staff and the presidential library.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:56.470
Maybe they have to fundraise for the presidential
library.

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:58.980
Now, I don't that I don't remember.

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:03.060
But the point is, in terms of the pension,
it's not mandatory.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:11.670
So is Trump just so greedy and so cheap that
he won't turn anything down and he'll go through

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:16.190
the process of getting something that is the
equivalent at his net worth of three dollars

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:20.370
and 40 cents for a person of average or median
net worth?

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:25.360
Maybe he needs the money because a lot of
that net worth is completely illiquid.

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:26.480
Is he desperate?

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:27.480
I don't know.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:33.160
We've talked about those controversial loans
that we knew would start to come due during

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:34.990
what would have been his second term.

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:38.340
And thankfully is not because he lost.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:42.530
Maybe that's related, but I find that there's
something sort of strange about it.

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:43.530
And maybe it's as simple.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.900
I mean, let me know what you think.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:53.110
Maybe it really is as simple as Donald Trump
just can't turn any money down because of

00:03:53.110 --> 00:03:56.790
his personality and because of who he is.

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:57.830
Maybe there's some other explanation.

00:03:57.830 --> 00:03:58.830
I don't know.

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:06.280
But billionaire multibillionaire Donald Trump
going through the process of requesting, filing

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:13.900
for and obtaining what is for his level of
net worth, equivalent to three dollars worth

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:17.850
of a federal presidential pension for ex presidents.

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:20.590
Am I the only one finding something weird
about that?

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:44.970
Let me know.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:45.180
T

